1515732.steps:
1).Login to the FW as admin from the default LAN interface;
2).Navigate to Network&gt;Interfaces, open the configure dialog of the default LAN, select the Layer 2 Bridged Mode from the IP assignment dropdown box, make sure the contents on the page change;
3).Make sure there is a new dropdown box Bridged to, expand it and make sure all interfaces listed in it;
4).Make sure there are three new checkboxes Block all non-IPv4 traffic, Never route traffic on this bridge-pair and Only sniff traffic on this bridge-pair list below the dropdown box;
5).Make sure there is a new tab VLAN Filtering appeared after switching to Layer2 Bridged Mode;

1515741.steps:
1).Login to the Firewall from default LAN interface; 
2).Navigate to Network&gt;Interface page, enter the configure dialog of interface X1, make sure the X1 interface is assigned to WAN zone, and there are 11 items in General tab: Zone, IP Assignment, IP Address, Subnet Mask, Default Gateway, DNS Server 1, DNS Server2, DNS Server3, Comment, Management, and User Login;
3).Make sure the zone of the interface X1 can be changed, and the drop-down box includes 6 items: Unassigned, Create new Zone, LAN, WAN, DMZ and WLAN; 
4).Make sure there are 5 choice for the IP Assignment: Static, DHCP, PPPoE, PPTP and L2TP, the default choice is Static;
(Note: During GEN7 test, the default choice is changed to DHCP)
5).Make sure the default IP address is "0.0.0.0", the default Gateway is "0.0.0.0" and the default subnet mask is "255.255.255.0"; 
6).Make sure there are 3 DNS server fields, the default values are "0.0.0.0"; 
7).Make sure there is no item checked as default in Management in User Login, and the Comment is "Default WAN"; 
8).Go to the Advance tab, and make sure there are 2 sections: Advanced Settings and Bandwidth Management; 
9).In Advanced Settings section, make sure there are Link Speed, MAC Address, Multicast Support, 802.1p tagging, and MTU; 
10).For Link Speed drop-down box, make sure there are 6 items: 10 Mbps-Half Duplex, 10 Mbps-Full Duplex, 100 Mbps-Half Duplex, 100 Mbps-Full Duplex, 1000Mbps-Full Duplex and Auto Negotiate, and the default choice is "Auto Negotiate";
11).For MAC Address, there are two radios "Use Default MAC Address" and "Override Default MAC Address", the default choice is the first one; 
12).The checkboxes of Multicast Support and 802.1p tagging are unchecked as default. 
13).For the MTU, the default value of Interface MTU field is 1500, and make sure there are 3 checkboxes for Interface MTU, the first one is checked by default; 
14).In Bandwidth Management section, there are two checkbox "Enable Egress Bandwidth Management" and "Enable Ingress Bandwidth Management", under each of them, there are two edit boxes "Available Interface Egress Bandwidth" and "Available Interface Ingress Bandwidth".

1515749.steps:
1).Login to the FW as admin from the default LAN interface; 
2).Navigate to Network&gt;Interfaces page, on the default WAN interface edit dialog, configure default WAN to DHCP mode and apply; 
3).After the WAN interface get DHCP IP address, press the Release button on WAN config dialog, make sure the FW sends DHCP release packets, the assigned IP info are reset to 0.0.0.0 and log prints "Sending DHCP RELEASE"; 
4).After the DHCP assigned info are released, press the Renew button on Interface setting table or WAN config dialog, make sure the FW sends DHCP Discover and Request packets, and receives DHCP assigned IP address again; 
5).Press the Refresh button, and make sure the old info displayed on WAN interface config dialog will be updated;

1515752.steps:
1).Login to the Firewall from default LAN interface;
2).Navigate to Network&gt;Interfaces page, and open the configure dialog of the default LAN interface; 
3).Change the default IP to "0.0.0.0", and make sure there is a dialog pop-up reminding to enter an IP address; 
4).Input a string into the "IP Address" field, make sure the change isn't applied with an error report as "Error: Data is incorrectly formatted"; 
5).Input invalid IP address with one of the octets larger than 255, such as "1.1.1.256", make sure the change isn't applied with an error report as "Error: Data is incorrectly formatted"
6).Input an IP address with the first octet equal to 255, such a "255.1.1.1", make sure the change isn't applied with an error message "Error: Invalid IP Address"; 
7).Input an IP address with the last octet equal to 255, such a "1.1.1.255", make sure the change isn't applied with an error message "Error: Invalid IP Address-Choose an address within the subnet"; 
8).Input a valid IP address, and make sure the FW accept the change; 
9).Repeat the test steps on other interfaces assigned to WAN/DMZ/WLAN zone with static IP assignment.

